// ============================================================================
// FantasyStakes marketing site - Cloudflare Workers Static Assets
//
// WHAT THIS DEPLOYS. The static marketing site in ./site, and nothing else.
// There is no Worker script: an assets-only Worker serves the directory
// directly from Cloudflare's edge, which is what a site with no backend, no
// build step and no dependencies actually needs.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL. Cloudflare's current dashboard exposes the
// Worker Git deployment flow rather than the Pages project flow, and that flow
// reads its configuration from the repository instead of from dashboard fields.
// The three keys below are the whole configuration.
//
// DELIBERATELY ABSENT, each one a thing that would be wrong here:
//
//   main            no Worker script exists; naming one would fail the build
//   assets.binding  only meaningful when a Worker script needs to fetch assets
//                   programmatically, which requires `main`
//   pages_build_output_dir
//                   Pages-only, and this is a Worker
//   site / bucket   the deprecated Workers Sites model, superseded by `assets`
//   account_id      an account identifier is a credential-adjacent value and
//                   belongs in the dashboard or the environment, never in a
//                   committed file
//   routes / custom domains
//                   WEB-2a is preview only. fantasystakesapp.com is NOT
//                   attached here, and no DNS is touched.
//
// `_headers` and `_redirects` live inside ./site and are read by Workers Static
// Assets from the assets directory; they are applied as configuration rather
// than served as files, so the security headers and the www rule certified in
// WEB-1 carry over unchanged.
// ============================================================================
{
  "name": "fantasystakes-marketing",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-08-19",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./site"
  }
}
